{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/android/debug_keystore.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328799Z","id":"50df1c587bf774a97810a5076c7799fef0cfa586f3a8c4a45e5eed0011baa319","body":{"detail":"As apps/clax_app/android/app/build.gradle.kts signs its release build with the debug key, so an APK built by either installs over one already on the owner's phone (same certificate SHA-256 9874f8473ebc181beb90c6af8b4d29dfac87a97bcde62da0880a71938d28ce85 for the Gradle-built and the Bazel-built APK, 2026-10-17, apksigner verify --print-certs). The repository rule is local and watches the file; the APK targets are no-remote. Without the file (CI) rules_android's own key signs, and that APK does not install over a developer's. Accepted until the app has a release key.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"59247bf5fac45ba00942e592f3384bc8473401becee37f251b0e8dc1841627c3"},"summary":"The APK is signed with this machine's ~/.android/debug.keystore, an input Bazel does not pin","tags":["apk","signing","revisit:the app gets a release signing key","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/android/maven_install.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.086964Z","id":"c8a42da08cc0c9f52697dc1cb343c963be3121b0d5cbeb32ff98c06724aed2c7","body":{"detail":"LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only. bazel cquery 'deps(//apps/clax_app:apk)' reaches androidx.core, activity, fragment, lifecycle, media, webkit, window and others (Apache-2.0; the APK carries META-INF/androidx/*/LICENSE.txt), org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib and kotlinx-coroutines and kotlinx-serialization (Apache-2.0), com.getkeepsafe.relinker (Apache-2.0), com.google.crypto.tink:tink-android (Apache-2.0, flutter_secure_storage), and com.google.android.gms:play-services-location, -base, -basement and -tasks (line 203; geolocator_android; Google's proprietary Android SDK license). They are dexed into the same APK as the app's Kotlin (MainActivity). GPLv2's system-library exception covers the platform's android.jar but arguably not libraries bundled in the APK. Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries, and one for Google Play services or other non-free platform libraries; (b) for Play services, have geolocator use Android's LocationManager only (its forceLocationManager setting still links the library) or replace geolocator; AndroidX and Kotlin cannot practically be replaced in a Flutter Android app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"eecea05e1ea12e04ea4eaadbfbc4ff576963fae544bdbc044ccde54e8dd11189"},"summary":"The APK ships AndroidX, Kotlin's standard library and kotlinx, relinker and Tink (Apache-2.0) and Google Play services location (Android SDK license) with GPL-2.0-only code","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/android/maven_install.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:13.954028Z","id":"e9de0c93cb956a67a9b6d82114f3f5fc5c45320a489cb80d717db6457a29863a","body":{"detail":"LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only. bazel cquery 'deps(//apps/clax_app:apk)' reaches androidx.core, activity, fragment, lifecycle, media, webkit, window and others (Apache-2.0; the APK carries META-INF/androidx/*/LICENSE.txt), org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib and kotlinx-coroutines and kotlinx-serialization (Apache-2.0), com.getkeepsafe.relinker (Apache-2.0), com.google.crypto.tink:tink-android (Apache-2.0, flutter_secure_storage), and com.google.android.gms:play-services-location, -base, -basement and -tasks (line 203; geolocator_android; Google's proprietary Android SDK license). They are dexed into the same APK as the app's Kotlin (MainActivity). GPLv2's system-library exception covers the platform's android.jar but arguably not libraries bundled in the APK. Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries, and one for Google Play services or other non-free platform libraries; (b) for Play services, have geolocator use Android's LocationManager only (its forceLocationManager setting still links the library) or replace geolocator; AndroidX and Kotlin cannot practically be replaced in a Flutter Android app.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"eecea05e1ea12e04ea4eaadbfbc4ff576963fae544bdbc044ccde54e8dd11189"},"summary":"The APK ships AndroidX, Kotlin's standard library and kotlinx, relinker and Tink (Apache-2.0) and Google Play services location (Android SDK license) with GPL-2.0-only code","supersedes":"c8a42da08cc0c9f52697dc1cb343c963be3121b0d5cbeb32ff98c06724aed2c7","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
